<title>NETHERLANDS: POLL - Dutch May-July unemployment seen lower.</title>
<headline>POLL - Dutch May-July unemployment seen lower.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch economists forecast a slight fall in both seasonally adjusted and non-seasonally adjusted unemployment for the May-July period, according to a regular Reuters poll.</p>
<p>One contributor said strong exports and buoyant domestic consumer demand were continuing to fuel demand for labour.</p>
<p>Economists' forecasts are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period---Indicator---------Consensus--Range----Pvs  0730  19/8  May-July Unemployment NSA  375,000    370-381  376</p>
<p> 0730  19/8  May-July Unemployment SA   389,000    385-397  395</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, Generale Bank, ING, MeesPierson, J.P. Morgan, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
